# What tools/build-zip.sh leaves out of the release zip (rsync --exclude-from), and, line for line, what .gitattributes
# marks export-ignore, so git archive and GitHub's "Source code (zip)" hold the same files (gate 19, D-346).
# The dotfile lines are a second safeguard: build-zip.sh drops every dotfile and then checks that none is left. They
# stay so the two lists agree, and so a dotfile is still left out if that rule is ever changed.
# composer.json is not here: the zip ships it beside vendor/, so a reviewer can see what vendor/ holds.
.git
.github
.githooks
.claude
.idea
.vscode
.distignore
